From 2c2b9cb61f9cdae0a1eb18126dbec4df702b8aeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael <lukakcollwarm@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:29:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(notifications): add a Show message previews setting

Notifications showed message text in the list and the detail view, so
anyone who could see the screen could read private messages. Add a
'Show message previews' switch to Settings > Notifications (on by
default, saved on this device).

When it is off, the list and detail show only who sent it and what
happened ('Sent you a message', 'Mentioned you in #general',
'New message in #design'); the message is read in the conversation.

- summarizeNotification() builds the content-free line from the payload
  and never falls back to a title that looks like the message
- useShowMessagePreviews() keeps every open view in sync, across tabs
- node:test unit tests for the summary text
